            "id": "4945659",
            "title": "FOMC Meeting Takes Centre Stage As Earnings Fade",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\">Get ahead of the market by subscribing to Seeking Alpha's Wall Street Week Ahead, a preview of key events scheduled for the coming week. The newsletter keeps you informed of the biggest stories set to make headlines, including upcoming IPOs, investor days, earnings reports, and conference presentations.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Wall Street’s major averages pushed higher Friday after the latest consumer inflation report came in largely in line with expectations. U.S. consumer prices rose 0.4% in August, matching forecasts after a 0.1% gain in July and leaving the year-over-year rate unchanged at 3.4%. Core CPI (ex-food and energy) increased 0.3% versus the 0.2% consensus and prior reading, while the annual core rate eased to 2.4% from 2.5%, in line with estimates.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">The economic calendar is light for the upcoming week barring the Federal Reserve’s interest rate decision, which is due on Wednesday. August’s retail sales data will also be released on the same day. The FOMC will hold its press conference the following day, with initial jobless claims data and the Philadelphia Fed Manufacturing Index for September also scheduled for Thursday.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">VinFast (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VFS\" title=\"VinFast Auto Ltd.\">VFS</a>) is among the firms reporting in the coming week.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">______________________________________________________________</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Earnings spotlight:</b> Friday: VinFast (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VFS\" title=\"VinFast Auto Ltd.\">VFS</a>). <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/earnings/earnings-calendar#hasComeFromMpArticle=false\" target=\"_blank\">See the full earnings calendar</a>.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Volatility watch: </b>Amazon (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMZN\" title=\"Amazon.com, Inc.\">AMZN</a>) and Super Micro Computer (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SMCI\" title=\"Super Micro Computer, Inc.\">SMCI</a>) have seen options volatility increase over the last week. The most overbought stocks per their 14-day Relative Strength Index include TJGC Group (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TJGC\" title=\"TJGC Group Limited\">TJGC</a>), Cascadia Minerals (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CAMNF\" title=\"Cascadia Minerals Ltd.\">CAMNF</a>), and Private Bancorp of America (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PBAM\" title=\"Private Bancorp of America, Inc.\">PBAM</a>). The most oversold stocks per their 14-day Relative Strength Index include EverCommerce (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/EVCM\" title=\"EverCommerce Inc.\">EVCM</a>) and Burlington Stores (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/BURL\" title=\"Burlington Stores, Inc.\">BURL</a>). Short interest is elevated on Vital Farms (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VITL\" title=\"Vital Farms, Inc.\">VITL</a>) and Hims &amp; Hers (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/HIMS\" title=\"Hims &amp; Hers Health, Inc.\">HIMS</a>).</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Dividend watch:</b> Companies that have an ex-dividend date coming next week include FedEx (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FDX\" title=\"FedEx Corporation\">FDX</a>), UnitedHealth Group (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/UNH\" title=\"UnitedHealth Group Incorporated\">UNH</a>), Altria (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MO\" title=\"Altria Group, Inc.\">MO</a>), and Coca-Cola (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/KO\" title=\"The Coca-Cola Company\">KO</a>).</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>IPO watch:</b> Companies due to price their</p></body></html>",
